   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 20 of the laws of 1985 creating the Sanborn Volunteer\nand Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, Inc., and providing for its\npowers and duties, in relation to its purpose and the use of foreign fire\ninsurance premiums",
    "basePrintNo": "S1139",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1139-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§3 & 7, Chap 20 of 1985",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Assoc., Inc.",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1139\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 20 of the laws of 1985 creating the Sanborn\nVolunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, Inc., and provid-\ning for its powers and duties, in relation to its purpose and the use of\nforeign fire insurance premiums\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Sanborn Volunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Asso-\nciation to provide the relief, aid and assistance of members and their\nfamilies who are injured.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 3 is amended to change the purpose of the association to provide\nthe relief, aid and assistance of such members and their families who\nare injured, disabled or indigent. To promote and safeguard the welfare\nof the volunteer members of the corporation and their families; to\nprovide for the health and safety of the volunteer members of the corpo-\nration and to enhance the morale of the volunteer members of the corpo-\nration by providing social and recreational activities for the volunteer\nmembers of the corporation.\n\nSection 7 is amended to fix a technical error.\n\nSubsection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVolunteer firefighters perform dangerous duties each and every day in\nour communities. They offer reliable protection to our health, well\nbeing and property. They receive no compensation for their efforts\nexcept our heartfelt thanks and a small \"pension like\" benefit after\nyears of service.\n\nThese changes were requested by the Sanborn Volunteer and Exempt Fire-\nmen's Benevolent Association and are identical to language found in the\nformation of the Cold Spring Harbor Fire Benevolent Association in 2018\nand the revision of the existing association in North Tarrytown in 2019.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: S. 7413 Passed Senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
